               </respStmt>
            </titleStmt>
            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_N20319">
               <extent xml:id="extent_N2031A">4 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_N2031D">27.4 x 38</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_N20320">Written in black ink. Paper: 10 staves. Above the music: "Aandelige Sange af I.P.E. Hartmann." At the end of the music: "Comp. i Sommeren 1870." (Composed during the summer of 1870). Beneath the music Liebmann has written: "(Opskreven efter Hukommelsen og derfor maaske paa sine Steder mindre correct.)"  (Written down from memory and thus in some places perhaps less correct.). In fact there are only very few slips of the mind, mainly in the accompaniment.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
            <notesStmt xml:id="notesStmt_N20322">
               <annot type="source_description" xml:id="annot_3194db56">
                  <p xml:id="idm58">Contains "O, lad din Aand nu med os være" (HartW 425), "Hører du Røsten" (HartW 416) and "O, du Guds Lam".</p>
